  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=-1\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=\\pi +x=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
